  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bell Textron has $2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Bell Textron has 766 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2.6M. Bell Textron obligations are up 30.1% year over year. Bell Textron received $1.9B from the Department of Defense and $53.2M from the Department of the Interior in FY2026 to date. Bell Textron sells primarily in Aircraft Manufacturing, which accounts for $1.8B of obligations, and in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing, which accounts for $165M. Bell Textron also shows smaller FY2026 to date activity in markets such as Scale and Balance Manufacturing at $1.6M and Engineering Services at $635K. Historical obligations for Bell Textron rose from $349M in FY21 to $2B in FY26, showing higher nominal annual obligations in recent years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Bell Textron's federal contracting trended over recent years?",
        "body": "Obligations for Bell Textron grew from $349M in FY21 to $2B in FY26. Obligations for Bell Textron were $307M in FY22, $985M in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, and $1.5B in FY25. Obligations for Bell Textron are up 30.1% year over year for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Bell Textron's largest government customers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer from Bell Textron at $1.9B in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Interior is the next largest at $53.2M, with smaller amounts from the Department of Justice at $362K, the Department of Transportation at $135K, and the Department of Energy at $58.5K. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Bell Textron at $1.8B, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $165M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Bell Textron make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Bell Textron makes $2B from federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Bell Textron has 766 awards this fiscal year to date and an average award size of $2.6M."
